+# AI #12 — findings register (onboarding & help lane)
+
+Branch `arena/145e7090-ledgerflow`, based on `main` `bce500c`. Every entry below was found in this
+session unless marked otherwise; each one names the file, the evidence, what it costs the person
+using the product, how to see it again, whether it is fixed, and which test holds it fixed.
+
+Severity is about what a real user loses: **S1** wrong information or a broken money-adjacent path,
+**S2** a screen that misleads or refuses work, **S3** confusing or unreachable UI, **S4** hygiene.
+
+| ID | Sev | Where | What was wrong | Consequence | Repro | Status | Test |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| AI12-N10-01 | S2 | `src/core/auth/AuthScreen.tsx`, `NewPasswordScreen.tsx` | Sign-in, sign-up and password screens switched the page to Hebrew/RTL but printed English copy (plus English `aria-label`s and password errors). | A reader who chose Hebrew was given an English form in a mirrored layout — the first screen of the product. | Set `lf_language=he`, open `/`; the form read "Create Account" in an RTL page. | Fixed `6dcb990` | `src/tests/onboarding-hebrew.test.tsx`, `src/tests/onboarding-translation-guard.test.ts` |
+| AI12-N10-02 | S2 | `src/components/onboarding/SetupWizard.tsx` | The whole first-run wizard (business step, chart step, done step, error messages) was English-only in Hebrew. | The person who just signed up in Hebrew could not read the screen that creates their books. | Wizard in Hebrew mode. | Fixed `6dcb990` | `src/tests/setup-wizard.test.tsx`, `src/tests/setup-wizard-journey.test.tsx` |
+| AI12-N10-03 | S2 | `src/components/onboarding/FirstHourGuide.tsx`, `src/components/dashboard/FirstWeekChecklist.tsx` | The Overview's two first-run guides were English-only; the progress sentence ("0 of 5 steps complete") had no Hebrew form. | The "what do I do now" guidance — the reason a new owner gets anywhere — was unreadable in Hebrew. | Overview in Hebrew mode. | Fixed `6dcb990` | `src/tests/first-hour-guide.test.tsx`, `src/tests/first-week-checklist.test.tsx` |
+| AI12-N10-04 | S4 | `src/lib/i18n/onboardingTranslations.ts` (as first written) | The copy table repeated every English sentence as an inline fallback argument in each screen. Entry chunk 246,510 B → 276,789 B, over the 260,000 B bootstrap budget; CI Production build failed on `stage6-footprint-optimization` case 3. | Every visitor downloads ~30 KB more on first paint, and the release gate blocks the branch. | `LF_REQUIRE_BUILT_DIST=1 npx tsx --test src/tests/stage6-footprint-optimization.test.ts` after `npm run build`. | Fixed `b5b70ec` (256,287 B) | `src/tests/stage6-footprint-optimization.test.ts` |
+| AI12-N10-05 | S2 | `src/components/onboarding/SetupWizard.tsx` | The suggested-labels sentence was rendered before a business type was chosen, with `None` substituted, and still claimed "Fund is self-balancing for a new non-profit label". In Hebrew it also kept the English word `Fund`. | Every new user, both languages, was told a fund existed and explained a label that was not there — then chose their business type and found the sentence changed. | Open the wizard step 1 and read the line under "What kind of business?" without choosing anything. | Fixed `d91eaec` | `src/tests/setup-wizard.test.tsx` ("the suggested-labels sentence names the chosen preset…") |
+| AI12-N10-06 | S4 | `e2e/onboarding-hebrew.spec.ts` (as first written) | The Latin-word check counted `<option>` text, so the currency list (USD, EUR, …) and the IANA time-zone list (800+ entries) counted as English copy on a correct Hebrew screen; a second test asserted `<html lang>` in a fixture that mounts the wizard alone. | The spec failed on correct behaviour — noise that would have hidden a real regression later. | Browser shard 2/5 on `d91eaec`. | Fixed `505fbeb` | the spec itself (CI) |
+| AI12-N10-07 | S4 | `src/lib/i18n/onboardingTranslations.ts` + the two screen tables + the spec | Three tables each carried the same lookup/fallback/row-builder/gap-scan code, and the Hebrew-wizard mount was copy-pasted in the spec. | Three places to keep in step, and SonarCloud's "Duplication on New Code" gate failing on the PR. | `npx jscpd --min-lines 10 --min-tokens 100` over the changed files: 1 clone before, 0 after. | Fixed `dec5633` | `src/tests/onboarding-translation-guard.test.ts` ("the shared table reader behaves the same for every table") |
+| AI12-N3-01 | S2 | `src/lib/errorRemedies.ts`, `src/lib/runCommand.ts`, `src/lib/utils.ts`, 40+ call sites | Every failed save/load told the user what to do in English only, even in Hebrew, while the rest of the page was Hebrew. | The one moment a person needs the words most — a refusal — was in a language they did not choose. | `describeError(err, 'create')` ignored the UI language. | Fixed `cd70dd1` | `src/tests/error-remedies-hebrew.test.tsx` (13) |
+| AI12-N8-01 | S4 | `e2e/` (nothing spanning the four first-run screens) | Each first-run screen had its own spec, but no test walked setup → first invoice → Overview, the seam where the checklist must notice what the wizard and the invoice form produced. | A regression in the hand-off between screens (a step counted from the wrong signal) would pass every existing spec. | — (gap, not a defect) | Added `3c3138b` | `e2e/onboarding-first-invoice.spec.ts` |
+
+## Out of scope, reported not patched
+
+- Anything under `src/server/**`, `supabase/migrations/**`, money/tax maths, statements/PDFs belongs
+  to AI #1. Nothing in this branch touches those paths (verified by `git diff --name-only`).
